# Course 6 (LODE; docs/plans/bonanza-courses/LODE.md): LODESTONE GORGE, STEEL's course - a SPIRAL into a
# quarry round the GREAT LODESTONE, on an island in its middle.  The FLUME (an S of round channel between stone
# curbs, 6.5 units down), a HOIST (a magnet at a ramp's top hauls steel up it), the SIRENS (magnets across a gap
# that pull steel off a bridge), a ramp into the LODESTONE WALL (a tilted ledge a fence of magnets holds steel
# on), the SLAG gallery (a room to stop in), the GANTRY (a row of hanging magnets steel HOVERS under, over the
# moat), and the great lodestone's own hoist, into the goal.  REFINED (2026-11-25, the step after the pen-in):
# written by docs/plans/bonanza-courses/lode/sketch.py --bbc --force while the layout moves.  NOT in the build
# yet (no BZ_COURSES entry, no pathway pad).
course LODE "Lodestone Gorge"
guide                     # a REAL course: held to the course guide's checkable rules (G1, G3, G9 - G12)
width 104                 # 832 px: the reach runs from px 8 (the void off the gallery's west corner) to 791 (off the turn)
origin 272                # NOT free: the least the reach allows, so the picture's LEFT EDGE is 112 px from the gallery's
                          # pocket - the window cannot pan further left, which is what frames the gantry's flight with
                          # no pan (LODE.md section 2).  A wider picture takes `width`; the origin stays
ball steel
uses magnet
music lodestone           # its own song (2026-11-25): a work song in G dorian, every bar pulled back to one low G (LODE.md, "The song")
limit 99
target 60

# rooms (the sketch's sections), walls and guard rails
floor rect  20   4  25   8  flat 22.5   # A: the HEADLAND, 5 x 4
guard rect  20   4  25   5 side -y
guard rect  20   4  21   8 side -x
guard rect  24   4  25   8 side +x
wall  rect  20   8  21   9  flat 23   # the flume's curbs: the mouth's flanks
wall  rect  24   8  25   9  flat 23
wall  rect  20   9  21  13  ramp y 9 13 23 19   # the first leg's west curb, sloping with it
wall  rect  24   9  25  14  ramp y 9 14 23 18   # ...and its east curb
wall  rect  20  13  21  14  flat 19   # (the far curb's end, at the first leg's lip)
wall  rect  24  14  25  17  flat 18   # the first corner: its east side
wall  rect  21  17  24  18  flat 18   # ...and its outside
wall  rect  18  17  21  18  ramp x 18 21 16.5 18   # the middle leg's near curb
wall  rect  18  13  20  14  ramp x 18 20 16.5 17.5   # ...and its far curb
wall  rect  15  13  18  14  flat 16.5   # the second corner: its north side
wall  rect  14  14  15  18  flat 16.5   # ...and its outside, down the last leg
floor rect  14  18  24  25  flat 16   # B: the CATCH PEN, 10 x 7
guard rect  14  18  15  25 side -x
guard rect  14  24  24  25 side +y
guard rect  23  18  24  21 side +x
guard rect  23  23  24  25 side +x
floor rect  24  21  26  23  flat 16   # the hoist's foot, off the pen's east side
floor rect  25  19  26  21  ramp y 19 21 18 16   # H: the HOIST's ramp, 2 units in 2 tiles: steel stalls on it
floor rect  25  18  26  19  flat 18   # its top
floor rect  25  17  26  18  flat 20   # the hoist's post
guard rect  24  22  26  23 side +y
guard rect  25  21  26  23 side +x
guard rect  25  19  26  21 side -x +x
guard rect  25  18  26  19 side -x
guard rect  24  21  25  22 side -y
floor rect  26  18  43  20  flat 18   # C: the SIRENS' bridge, 17 x 2
floor rect  31  15  32  16  flat 20   # a siren's pillar
floor rect  35  22  36  23  flat 20   # a siren's pillar
floor rect  39  15  40  16  flat 20   # a siren's pillar
floor rect  43  18  46  23  flat 18   # P: the TURN, 3 x 5
guard rect  43  18  46  19 side -y
guard rect  45  18  46  23 side +x
guard rect  43  20  44  23 side -x
guard rect  43  22  45  23 side +y
floor rect  45  23  46  28  ramp y 23 28 18 13   # R: the ramp, 5 units in 5 tiles, 1 wide and railed: the speed for the wall
guard rect  45  23  46  28 side +x -x
floor rect  45  28  46  33  flat 13   # L: the ledge, 1 wide, level and railed
guard rect  45  28  46  33 side +x -x
floor rect  45  33  46  39  ramp x 45 46 13.25 12.75   # L: the LODESTONE WALL's first leg: tilted to its open side
floor rect  45  39  46  41  flat 13   # the wall's corner
guard rect  45  39  46  41 side +x +y
guard rect  45  39  46  40 side -x
floor rect  43  40  45  41  flat 13   # the second leg's lead-in: level and railed, as the first leg's ledge is
guard rect  43  40  45  41 side -y +y
floor rect  37  40  43  41  ramp y 40 41 13.25 12.75   # L: its second leg, walked up-left (-x)
floor rect  44  33  45  34  flat 15   # a lodestone's post
floor rect  44  34  45  35  flat 15   # a lodestone's post
floor rect  44  35  45  36  flat 15   # a lodestone's post
floor rect  44  36  45  37  flat 15   # a lodestone's post
floor rect  44  37  45  38  flat 15   # a lodestone's post
floor rect  44  38  45  39  flat 15   # a lodestone's post
floor rect  37  39  38  40  flat 15   # a lodestone's post
floor rect  38  39  39  40  flat 15   # a lodestone's post
floor rect  39  39  40  40  flat 15   # a lodestone's post
floor rect  40  39  41  40  flat 15   # a lodestone's post
floor rect  41  39  42  40  flat 15   # a lodestone's post
floor rect  42  39  43  40  flat 15   # a lodestone's post
floor rect  30  39  37  42  flat 13   # S: the SLAG gallery, 7 x 3
guard rect  30  39  31  42 side -x
guard rect  30  41  37  42 side +y
guard rect  31  39  37  40 side -y
guard rect  36  41  37  42 side +x
floor rect  30  37  31  39  flat 13   # Y: the RUNWAY, 1 wide, railed both sides: the ball leaves it straight
guard rect  30  37  31  39 side -x +x
floor rect  29  32  30  33  flat 14.5   # the gantry's post
floor rect  29  33  30  34  flat 14.5   # the gantry's post
floor rect  29  34  30  35  flat 14.5   # the gantry's post
floor rect  29  35  30  36  flat 14.5   # the gantry's post
floor rect  29  36  30  37  flat 14.5   # the gantry's post
floor rect  28  29  33  32  flat 12.5   # V: the island's apron, 5 x 3
guard rect  28  29  29  32 side -x
guard rect  32  29  33  32 side +x
guard rect  28  31  30  32 side +y
guard rect  31  31  33  32 side +y
guard rect  28  29  30  30 side -y
guard rect  31  29  33  30 side -y
floor rect  30  26  31  29  ramp y 26 29 15.5 12.5   # the last ramp, 3 units in 3 tiles, railed both sides
guard rect  30  26  31  29 side -x +x
floor rect  30  24  31  25  flat 17.5   # the GREAT LODESTONE's post

chute 3 round depth 6 way 22 8 22.5 way 22 15 17.5 way 16 15 16 way 16 18 16
prop magnet 25 17 face +y range 3 strength 64
prop magnet 31 15 face +y range 4 strength 16
prop magnet 35 22 face -y range 4 strength 24
prop magnet 39 15 face +y range 4 strength 32
prop magnet 44 33 face +x strength 8
prop magnet 44 34 face +x strength 8
prop magnet 44 35 face +x strength 8
prop magnet 44 36 face +x strength 8
prop magnet 44 37 face +x strength 8
prop magnet 44 38 face +x strength 8
prop magnet 37 39 face +y strength 8
prop magnet 38 39 face +y strength 8
prop magnet 39 39 face +y strength 8
prop magnet 40 39 face +y strength 8
prop magnet 41 39 face +y strength 8
prop magnet 42 39 face +y strength 8
prop magnet 29 32 face down +x
prop magnet 29 33 face down +x
prop magnet 29 34 face down +x
prop magnet 29 35 face down +x
prop magnet 29 36 face down +x
prop magnet 30 24 face +y range 4 strength 104
# the cells no ball is in (LODE.md section 11): the void no fall reaches, and the tiles of the posts no ball gets onto
noocclude rect 17 1 28 4
noocclude rect 17 4 20 10
noocclude rect 25 4 28 12
noocclude rect 12 10 20 11
noocclude rect 11 11 20 13
noocclude rect 25 12 35 14
noocclude rect 36 12 43 14
noocclude rect 11 13 15 14
noocclude rect 11 14 14 25
noocclude rect 31 15 32 16
noocclude rect 39 15 40 16
noocclude rect 45 15 49 17
noocclude rect 24 17 26 18
noocclude rect 44 17 49 18
noocclude rect 24 18 25 21
noocclude rect 46 18 49 31
noocclude rect 35 22 36 23
noocclude rect 24 24 39 25
noocclude rect 40 24 45 26
noocclude rect 11 25 29 26
noocclude rect 32 25 39 26
noocclude rect 11 26 30 28
noocclude rect 31 26 36 29
noocclude rect 42 26 45 30
noocclude rect 25 28 30 29
noocclude rect 25 29 28 30
noocclude rect 33 29 36 30
noocclude rect 34 30 36 35
noocclude rect 41 30 45 36
noocclude rect 46 31 47 32
noocclude rect 34 36 45 39
noocclude rect 26 39 27 40
noocclude rect 37 39 45 40
noocclude rect 46 40 47 41
noocclude rect 27 41 30 42
noocclude rect 44 41 49 42
noocclude rect 27 42 35 45
noocclude rect 45 42 49 44
# ART (docs/plans/bonanza-courses/lode/art.py draws the files and places them: ART.md)
art lode_hoist.bba 310 320
art lode_sirens.bba 405 302
art lode_runway.bba 133 512
art lode_great.bba 341 376

goal  rect 29 25 32 26  flat 15.5
start 22 5
checkpoint 26 18 ball steel   # flag 0
checkpoint 36 40 ball steel   # flag 1

# clocks: on a corner of a floor off the way, or on a tile one out from it
clock 24 6 frame cart0   # start: empty
clock 14 19 frame cart1   # pen: a few lumps
clock 45 18 frame cart2   # turn: half full
clock 32 30 frame cart3   # vault: heaped

# the autopilot's route
way 22 5
way 22 8
way 22 15
way 16 15
way 16 18
way 17 21
way 22 21
way 25 21
way 25 18
way 26 18
way 42 19
way 44 20
way 45 23
way 45 28
way 45 40
way 44 40
way 36 40
way 30 40
way 30 37
way 30 30
way 30 29
way 30 25
